-- The width of a string: the crate's `str_width` and `str_width_cjk`.
--
-- A string is not the sum of its characters' widths: an emoji sequence joined
-- with ZWJ is one wide glyph, a variation selector changes the width of the
-- character before it, a lam-alef pair is one ligature, and so on. So the
-- string is read from the end with a little state -- what the characters after
-- this one have started -- and each character adds a width, which may be
-- negative, given that state.
--
-- This is a port of `width_in_str` and `width_in_str_cjk` in the crate's
-- `src/tables.rs`, arm for arm and in the same order. The two differ in a few
-- places, so they are one function here that takes `cjk`. The generator
-- refuses to run on a crate whose state machine differs from the one ported;
-- see `scripts/generate/src/main.rs`.
--
